{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you said to your servants: Bring him down.</b> Meaning: it did not suffice for you to verify the matter through our words or by some other investigation besides bringing him down to you, and you further pressed upon us that we not see your face without him. And we informed our father of the matter, and it did not help — he would not send him until the grain was exhausted, etc., and we were compelled to bring him down."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:35.420886373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}